scenarios.lede:
Accounting prints its aged balance to a spool file.
- a header on each page;
- a client, its invoices below, a total;
- a client's invoices sometimes run onto the next page.
Credit control wants each invoice with its client.

IT takes over an application inventory kept for years in a spreadsheet.
The URL column is typed by hand:
- mixed upper and lower case;
- stray spaces around it;
- a port sometimes there, sometimes not.
The manifest splits the URL into columns, without code.

Customers call: their order "never went through".
- the server writes a text log, one file a day;
- the ERP knows the orders, their customer, their status;
- no tool matches the two.
A business log, not a monitoring tool.

French banks still send statements in CFONB 120.
- 120 characters per record, no delimiter;
- 01 opens the statement, 04 is a movement, 05 completes it, 07 closes;
- the amount's last character holds its last digit and its sign.
Treasury wants each movement signed, with its complements.

The sales team leaves an old CRM. Its contact export mixes:
- capitals and broken accents (BÃ©nÃ©dicte);
- two phone columns, one often empty;
- mistyped emails.
The manifest turns it into a usable list.

A sales engineer has dinner with Lumilait's managing director. They must answer without opening four tools:
- the packaging line: ERP and after-sales disagree;
- the retrofit parts: in stock or not;
- the catalogue: 360 parts to search.
Meanwhile, the CRM marks the deal ready to confirm.

A real cluster, five teams, five pods broken by Kubernetes itself:
- the pods API: state, restarts, why the last container died;
- metrics.k8s.io: what each pod uses now;
- the Warning events.
An on-call Kotlin rule sets the priority; the model translates the question, it decides nothing.

The catalogue of approved versions is a CSV. What really runs is in the cluster. lumnik reads each pod's image through the Kubernetes API and joins it to the catalogue:
- the approved version passes;
- a hotfix pushed with kubectl set image makes the gate return exit code 1: CI stops the pipeline;
- after the rollback, the same command passes again.

An earlier provider left a stock application in Spring Data REST, behind nginx. lumnik reads it with the spring-hateoas preset:
- its links name its internal host: the run refuses to follow them, and says so;
- one property on the application side, and the 63 pages go through;
- each product is keyed by its SKU, read from its link: the next night, no second copy.
